'faqs'=>[['Can a child with high intelligence have dyslexia?','Yes. Dyslexia concerns specific reading and spelling processes, not overall intelligence. Strong reasoning or vocabulary may help a child compensate and delay recognition.'],['Is reversing letters a reliable dyslexia sign?','No. Letter reversals can occur during typical early writing. Clinicians consider persistent patterns across decoding, fluency, spelling, sound processing, instruction and educational history.'],['Can poor motivation cause dyslexia?','No. Avoidance and low confidence may develop after repeated reading difficulty. Assessment considers whether a skill problem is contributing before behaviour is labelled as laziness.'],['At what age can dyslexia be assessed?','Early reading risks can be identified before a child falls far behind. The assessment approach depends on age, instruction, language exposure and the referral question.']],
